From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 17:02:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS: guard bulk non-exec protect notifications on all three
 paths

FEX removes a range's executable intervals when told it is no longer
executable, so a >=1GB non-exec notification wipes the exec interval of
every module inside it. Suppress those before they reach the BTCpu module.

Guarded at all three call sites via one helper: NtProtectVirtualMemory's
pre and post notifications, and the ARM64EC cross-process work-list replay.
The replay path matters here specifically because our pseudo-processes
share one address space, so RtlIsCurrentProcess() is FALSE for a sibling
handle and the notification is queued rather than issued inline.

Defence in depth -- the real fix for the observed CEF failure is in FEX,
since that wipe arrived via NotifyMemoryAlloc (a pool reservation), not
via any protect call. A 16GB VirtualProtect would be equally bogus, so
this stays.

Also here: ec_code_map_limit() bounding the EC code bitmap, and the
[map-notify]/[unexec] probes used during the investigation.

(cherry picked from commit 71b042a5b63cc4b8cdd15e9f3bd91aea284c8271)
